.nh
.TH "TAKO" "1" "Jun 2026" "Tako CLI" "Tako CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
tako-aliases - List project command aliases from tako.yaml


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtako aliases [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List the project command aliases defined under "aliases:" in tako.yaml or
tako.json, with the Tako command each one runs.

.PP
Only the aliases section is read: no servers are contacted and environment
variables referenced elsewhere in the config are not required. Aliases whose
name matches a built-in command are reported as shadowed, because built-in
commands always take precedence.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for aliases


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	config file (default is ./tako.yaml or ./tako.json)

.PP
\fB-e\fP, \fB--env\fP=""
	environment to use (default: the only environment, else production, else the first alphabetically)

.PP
\fB--events\fP=""
	stream progress events to stdout: ndjson (human output moves to stderr)

.PP
\fB--host-key-mode\fP=""
	SSH host key verification mode: tofu, strict, ask (default: tofu)

.PP
\fB--output\fP="text"
	output format: text or json (json reserves stdout for the final result document)

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	verbose output


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  tako aliases
  tako aliases --output json
  tako --config ./deploy/tako.yaml aliases
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBtako(1)\fP
